{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "00271",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 1.05,
      "end_seconds": 3.92,
      "duration_seconds": 2.87,
      "text": "Sorry I'm a few minutes behind, doctor."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 5.07,
      "end_seconds": 7.99,
      "duration_seconds": 2.92,
      "text": "Right on time. Sit, please. How can I help?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 8.72,
      "end_seconds": 14.83,
      "duration_seconds": 6.11,
      "text": "So, doctor, I've come along because I know the history, if it helps."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 15.48,
      "end_seconds": 18.64,
      "duration_seconds": 3.16,
      "text": "Okay, good, that'll be useful. Pull up a chair."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 19.52,
      "end_seconds": 21.75,
      "duration_seconds": 2.23,
      "text": "He's been having fever, doctor."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 22.59,
      "end_seconds": 27.41,
      "duration_seconds": 4.82,
      "text": "How long have you had it? I'll explain everything as we go along."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 28.96,
      "end_seconds": 31.96,
      "duration_seconds": 3.0,
      "text": "Okay, so for ten days, I'd say."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 32.69,
      "end_seconds": 34.59,
      "duration_seconds": 1.9,
      "text": "And how severe is it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 38.4,
      "end_seconds": 39.99,
      "duration_seconds": 1.59,
      "text": "It's moderate, honestly."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 40.54,
      "end_seconds": 46.79,
      "duration_seconds": 6.25,
      "text": "Right, and the other thing I wanted to mention is that I can't really—"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 46.89,
      "end_seconds": 51.98,
      "duration_seconds": 5.09,
      "text": "Oh, tell the doctor about the other thing, that's what worries me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 52.71,
      "end_seconds": 54.71,
      "duration_seconds": 2.0,
      "text": "I was getting to that!"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 55.82,
      "end_seconds": 59.49,
      "duration_seconds": 3.67,
      "text": "That's fine, one at a time. I'll ask about everything."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 60.32,
      "end_seconds": 66.8,
      "duration_seconds": 6.48,
      "text": "Oh, and a runny nose. Oh, and a mild headache. Had that since this morning."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 67.43,
      "end_seconds": 70.72,
      "duration_seconds": 3.29,
      "text": "Does it happen all the time or in spells?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 72.04,
      "end_seconds": 79.03,
      "duration_seconds": 6.99,
      "text": "Hmm, it's, um... not exactly... well, hard to explain, I mean—"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 80.44,
      "end_seconds": 85.16,
      "duration_seconds": 4.72,
      "text": "Let me put it another way: how many times in a typical day or week?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 86.55,
      "end_seconds": 89.58,
      "duration_seconds": 3.03,
      "text": "It's a couple of times a week."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 91.15,
      "end_seconds": 92.75,
      "duration_seconds": 1.6,
      "text": "And how severe is it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 94.25,
      "end_seconds": 95.65,
      "duration_seconds": 1.4,
      "text": "It's severe, honestly."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 96.66,
      "end_seconds": 100.84,
      "duration_seconds": 4.18,
      "text": "Have you had fever before, or is this the first time?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 101.28,
      "end_seconds": 107.28,
      "duration_seconds": 6.0,
      "text": "A bit, about six months ago. It settled by itself back then."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "UNKNOWN",
      "start_seconds": 108.53,
      "end_seconds": 110.28,
      "duration_seconds": 1.75,
      "text": "Yes, exactly like that."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 110.94,
      "end_seconds": 112.78,
      "duration_seconds": 1.84,
      "text": "Has there been any rash?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 114.25,
      "end_seconds": 116.51,
      "duration_seconds": 2.26,
      "text": "Not at all, no rash."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 117.15,
      "end_seconds": 121.5,
      "duration_seconds": 4.35,
      "text": "Any shortness of breath, vomiting, stiff neck or chest pain at all?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 121.83,
      "end_seconds": 132.79,
      "duration_seconds": 10.96,
      "text": "No, no shortness of breath, no vomiting, no stiff neck. I did have body aches at one point, but that went away on its own."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 133.66,
      "end_seconds": 136.14,
      "duration_seconds": 2.48,
      "text": "Has there been any burning when passing urine?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 137.71,
      "end_seconds": 142.58,
      "duration_seconds": 4.87,
      "text": "Um, you know, no burning when passing urine, thank goodness."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_5",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 144.09,
      "end_seconds": 149.79,
      "duration_seconds": 5.7,
      "text": "Yeah, actually, doctor, I did notice burning when passing urine. He doesn't always say."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 150.14,
      "end_seconds": 155.99,
      "duration_seconds": 5.85,
      "text": "No, I don't think I did. Maybe a little, I'm not sure."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 157.49,
      "end_seconds": 163.09,
      "duration_seconds": 5.6,
      "text": "Alright, I'll note both what you've said and what you've noticed. Anything unusual with passing urine?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 164.15,
      "end_seconds": 165.99,
      "duration_seconds": 1.84,
      "text": "No, that's all fine."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 166.91,
      "end_seconds": 170.44,
      "duration_seconds": 3.53,
      "text": "Any medication at the moment, including things from the pharmacy?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 171.82,
      "end_seconds": 178.72,
      "duration_seconds": 6.9,
      "text": "It's a... um, I can't remember what it's called. It's a small white one."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 179.74,
      "end_seconds": 181.61,
      "duration_seconds": 1.87,
      "text": "Do you remember what it's for?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 182.49,
      "end_seconds": 200.04,
      "duration_seconds": 17.55,
      "text": "Yeah, for my blood pressure, I believe. My wife sets them out for me, I just take what I'm given. I take glimepiride, 2 milligrams, before breakfast for my sugar. I took the morning off to come in today."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 200.78,
      "end_seconds": 203.04,
      "duration_seconds": 2.26,
      "text": "How long have you been on it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 203.71,
      "end_seconds": 205.52,
      "duration_seconds": 1.81,
      "text": "About nearly five years."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 206.62,
      "end_seconds": 213.93,
      "duration_seconds": 7.31,
      "text": "What about your general health, any conditions you're being treated for? It helps to be thorough at this stage."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 214.6,
      "end_seconds": 240.46,
      "duration_seconds": 25.86,
      "text": "Well, you know, I have high blood pressure, for two years. My sister suggested writing things down, but I forgot. I've had diabetes, yes. I did try to ignore it for a while. So, I've had asthma for nearly five years now. I wasn't sure whether to come in at all, to be honest."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 244.23,
      "end_seconds": 250.35,
      "duration_seconds": 6.12,
      "text": "I see. Okay, diabetes, that's already on your record. Good to know. Does anything run in the family?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 251.72,
      "end_seconds": 255.77,
      "duration_seconds": 4.05,
      "text": "Yeah, my uncle had colon cancer. My mother has diabetes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 256.77,
      "end_seconds": 258.29,
      "duration_seconds": 1.52,
      "text": "Okay, any previous surgeries?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 258.99,
      "end_seconds": 267.98,
      "duration_seconds": 8.99,
      "text": "Yes, uh, I had cataract surgery on my right eye, last year. I'd rather know what's going on than keep guessing."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 269.37,
      "end_seconds": 270.36,
      "duration_seconds": 0.99,
      "text": "What about alcohol?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 273.65,
      "end_seconds": 277.6,
      "duration_seconds": 3.95,
      "text": "I have a couple of drinks on the weekend."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 278.37,
      "end_seconds": 279.09,
      "duration_seconds": 0.72,
      "text": "Any smoking?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0049",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 280.18,
      "end_seconds": 283.1,
      "duration_seconds": 2.92,
      "text": "I smoke about ten cigarettes a day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0050",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 284.28,
      "end_seconds": 291.73,
      "duration_seconds": 7.45,
      "text": "Right, do you have any allergies to medicines, food, anything at all? Just so I get the full picture."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0051",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 292.09,
      "end_seconds": 296.26,
      "duration_seconds": 4.17,
      "text": "Yeah, uh, no, none that I know of."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0052",
      "speaker_id": "person_6",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 296.63,
      "end_seconds": 308.26,
      "duration_seconds": 11.63,
      "text": "Here are the numbers, doctor. Height 170 centimetres, temperature 38.7, blood pressure 108 over 67. Pulse 108, weight 70 kilos, saturation 98 percent, BMI works out to 24.2."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0053",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 309.05,
      "end_seconds": 310.29,
      "duration_seconds": 1.24,
      "text": "Good, thank you."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0054",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 311.86,
      "end_seconds": 315.46,
      "duration_seconds": 3.6,
      "text": "Alright, I'd like to examine you now. Please come over here."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0055",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 316.46,
      "end_seconds": 319.11,
      "duration_seconds": 2.65,
      "text": "Okay, you know, go ahead."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0056",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 320.38,
      "end_seconds": 322.28,
      "duration_seconds": 1.9,
      "text": "Let me check your reflexes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0057",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 340.36,
      "end_seconds": 343.38,
      "duration_seconds": 3.02,
      "text": "Chest is clear when I listen, no crackles."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0058",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 344.79,
      "end_seconds": 347.57,
      "duration_seconds": 2.78,
      "text": "Turn your head to the side for me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0059",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 360.93,
      "end_seconds": 365.55,
      "duration_seconds": 4.62,
      "text": "Your throat looks red at the back, but there's no pus on the tonsils."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0060",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 370.67,
      "end_seconds": 390.53,
      "duration_seconds": 19.86,
      "text": "All done, thank you, please sit down. Okay, so my impression is this: This looks most like a viral upper respiratory infection. I want to be honest that this is an impression, not a final answer. It could also be influenza, so we'll keep that open. I'd also keep an early bacterial throat infection in mind."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0061",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 391.08,
      "end_seconds": 394.31,
      "duration_seconds": 3.23,
      "text": "Yeah, is this going to go away?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0062",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 397.55,
      "end_seconds": 410.18,
      "duration_seconds": 12.63,
      "text": "I can't promise yet, but most people with a viral upper respiratory infection do well once it's treated properly. We should do blood tests for fever. That will help us see what's going on underneath and decide the next step."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0063",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 410.66,
      "end_seconds": 414.02,
      "duration_seconds": 3.36,
      "text": "Uh, alright. When can I do that?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0064",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 415.53,
      "end_seconds": 436.59,
      "duration_seconds": 21.06,
      "text": "I'd like to arrange a flu swab for fever. The result will help us decide whether anything more is needed. I'd like to arrange a throat swab for sore throat. Let's use paracetamol, 500 milligrams, every six hours if needed, for three days. That's for fever and body aches. It's a commonly used medicine and most people tolerate it well."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0065",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 438.16,
      "end_seconds": 462.6,
      "duration_seconds": 24.44,
      "text": "I'm prescribing cetirizine, 10 milligrams, at night, for five days. That should help with blocked nose. I'll put all of this in writing so you don't have to remember it. Stay home, rest, and keep the fluids up. Warm soups and water, anything that goes down easily. A short walk every day, even twenty minutes, will help more than you'd think. Don't skip meals, and try to eat smaller portions more often through the day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0066",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 464.07,
      "end_seconds": 471.59,
      "duration_seconds": 7.52,
      "text": "Keep an eye out, and if the symptoms get worse, call us the same day or go to emergency."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0067",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 472.17,
      "end_seconds": 474.09,
      "duration_seconds": 1.92,
      "text": "Yes, I'll do that."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0068",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 474.9,
      "end_seconds": 479.63,
      "duration_seconds": 4.73,
      "text": "Let's review you in a week. Okay, I think we're finished. Is everything clear?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0069",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 480.55,
      "end_seconds": 483.61,
      "duration_seconds": 3.06,
      "text": "Oh, no, you've explained it well. Thanks."
    }
  ]
}